          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Nullstelle
            means
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+locus"} zero locus
            %em Nullstellensatz
            (theorem about zero loci) characterizes the joint zero loci of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            of functions in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            at the heart of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} duality
            by which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
            are dually interpreted as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/varieties"}> varieties
            ).
          %h2#classical_formulation_in_algebraic_geometry Classical formulation in algebraic geometry
          %p
            In classical algebraic geometry over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            of a standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideals"} ideals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subseteq k^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \perp V
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = 0
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in I, x \in V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Idl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idl(k[x_1, \ldots, x_n])
            be the set of ideals ordered by inclusion and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(k^n)
            the set of subsets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n
            ordered by inclusion, there are contravariant maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ideal
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Idl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ideal: P(k^n) \to Idl(k[x_1, \ldots, x_n])
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Var
                  %mo :
                  %mi Idl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Var: Idl(k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]) \to P(k^n)
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ideal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi x
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi Var
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi f
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ideal(S) = \{f \in k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]: \forall_x x \in S \Rightarrow f(x) = 0\}, \qquad Var(I) = \{x \in k^n: \forall_f f \in I \Rightarrow f(x) = 0\}
          %p which defines the Galois connection.
          %p
            The fixed points of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Var
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Ideal
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Var \circ Ideal: P(k^n) \to P(k^n)
            are, by definition, the closed sets of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n
            (“affine space” here in the sense of algebraic geometry). These are the closed (not necessarily reduced)
            %span.newWikiWord
              subvarieties
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/subvarieties"} ?
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n
          %p
            On the other side, the fixed points of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ideal
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi Var
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ideal \circ Var
            is what the classical Nullstellensatz is about:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Strong Nullstellensatz)
              The fixed points of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ideal
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi Var
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ideal \circ Var
              are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radical"} radical
              ideals
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              such that for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^r \in I
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in I
          %p
            Thus there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+correspondence"} Galois correspondence
            between closed subvarieties and radical ideals.
          %p Typically the way that the strong Nullstellensatz is proved is by reduction to the so-called “weak Nullstellensatz” by means of the “Rabinowitsch trick”. (The “weak” here may be misleading, as the weak Nullstellensatz may be considered the core result and the strong Nullstellensatz a corollary.) We now turn to these.
          %h3#ExistenceOfPoints A weak Nullstellensatz: Existence of points
          %p
            One weak version of the Nullstellensatz says the following (e.g. Theorem 3.99.1 here:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Frank-ALGANT-2010-7-12.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            a proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[X_1, \cdots, X_n]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(I)
            (of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = (x_i) \in k^n
            such that all polynomials in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            vanish when evaluated on these
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
          %p
            Before giving a proof, we remark (in view of more abstract formulations to come later) that an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(I)
            is just a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k \longleftarrow  k[X_1, \cdots, X_n]/I
                  \\,.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Dually
            this is a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"}> ring spectra
            ) of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Spec(k) \longrightarrow Spec(k[X_1, \cdots, X_n]/I)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(k)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in this context, such a map is the same as a “point”, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(k[X_1, \cdots, X_n]/I)
          %p
            Hence in this form the Nullstellensatz simply says that (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            algebraically closed) affine schemes have points. This formulation of the Nullstellensatz leads one to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GeneralAbstract"} more general abstract formulation
          %p We turn now to the proof of the weak Nullstellensatz.
          #uncountable.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is an
              %strong uncountable
              algebraically closed field, then for any proper ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]
              there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, \ldots, a_n) \in k^n
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a_1, \ldots, a_n) = 0
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in I
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is contained in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideal"} maximal ideal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = M
              is maximal, where we prove there is an isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi M
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]/M \cong k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ↠
                      %mi quot
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi M
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[X_1, \ldots, X_n] \stackrel{quot}{\twoheadrightarrow} k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]/M \stackrel{\phi}{\to} k
            %p
              sends each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              to a value
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_1 - a_1, \ldots, X_n - a_n) \subseteq M
            %p
              which must be an equality. In that case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, \ldots, a_n)
              is the desired point.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is algebraically closed, it suffices to prove that the extension field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]/M
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is algebraic over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              has countable
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in F
              that is transcendental over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotient"} subquotient
              vector space of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≅
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi k
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mi t
                              %mo −
                              %mi a
                          %mo ]
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{k(t)}{k[t]} \cong \bigoplus_{a \in k} \frac{k\left[\frac1{t - a}\right]}{k},
            %p
              where the isomorphism is by partial fraction decomposition (ultimately by the
              = succeed ")." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Chinese remainder theorem
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Chinese+remainder+theorem"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in k
          %p
            Now we reduce to the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is uncountable by employing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model-theoretic
            argument:
          #weak.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Weak Nullstellensatz)
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is an algebraically closed field, then for any proper ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]
              there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, \ldots, a_n) \in k^n
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a_1, \ldots, a_n) = 0
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in I
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              be a non-principal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilter"} ultrafilter
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultraproduct"} ultrapower
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi ℕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^\mathbb{N}/U
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Łoś's ultraproduct theorem
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%C5%81o%C5%9B%27s+ultraproduct+theorem"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is an algebraically closed field. Also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is uncountable (Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ultrapower"}
              below).
            %p
              First we claim
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \otimes_k I
              is a proper ideal of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \otimes_k k[X_1, \ldots, X_n] \cong K[X_1,\ldots, X_n]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = \sum_{i = 1}^s f_i p_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1, \ldots, p_s \in I
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i \in K[X_1, \ldots, X_n]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
              as
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\alpha
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_1, \ldots, q_t \in I
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\alpha p_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = \sum_{i=1}^t a_i q_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i = [(a_{i, m})] \in K
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_i \in I
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi in
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                    %mo ;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{m \in \mathbb{N}: 1 = \sum_{i=1}^t a_{i, m} q_i\; in\; k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]\} \in U;
            %p
              this set is nonempty, and so there is at least one
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              rendering the equation true. This contradicts
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \notin I
            %p
              By Lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#uncountable"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, \ldots, a_n) \in K^n
              belonging to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Var
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Var(K \otimes_k I)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noetherian+ring"} Hilbert's basis theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset k[X_1, \ldots, X_n]
              is generated by finitely many polynomials
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1, \ldots, p_s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Var
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Var(K \otimes_k I) \subseteq K^n
              is defined by finitely many formulas
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1(X) = 0, \ldots, p_s(X) = 0
              and thus by Łoś‘s theorem again,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi for
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{m \in \mathbb{N}: p_i(a_{1, m}, a_{2, m}, \ldots, a_{n, m}) = 0\; for\; i = 1, \ldots, s\} \in U
            %p
              and so this set is nonempty and therefore there is a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_{1, m}, \ldots, a_{n, m}) \in k^n
              that belongs to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Var
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Var(I)
          %p
            To prove
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            uncountable, we use the fact that an algebraically closed field is at least infinite. Then the missing piece is supplied by the following result.
          #ultrapower.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an infinite set and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is a non-principal ultrafilter on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\mathbb{N}/U
              has cardinality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℵ
                          %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X|}^{\aleph_0}
              (so at least
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℵ
                            %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{\aleph_0}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi i
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [j] = \{i \in \mathbb{N}: i \lt j\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is infinite, then there is a mono
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_j: X^{[j]} \to X
              for each
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \geq 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h: \mathbb{N} \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h|_{[j]}
              denote the composite
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi h
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [j] \hookrightarrow \mathbb{N} \stackrel{h}{\to} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h': \mathbb{N} \to X
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h'(j) = i_j(h|_{[j]})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [h']_U
              denote the value of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h'
              under the quotient map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi ℕ
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi ℕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\mathbb{N} \to X^\mathbb{N}/U
            %p
              Claim: The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\mathbb{N} \to X^\mathbb{N}/U
              that takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [h']_U
              is injective. For, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g, h: \mathbb{N} \to X
              are distinct, then they differ at some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi h
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g|_{[j]} \neq h|_{[j]}
              whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \lt j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_j(g|_{[j]}) \neq i_j(h|_{[j]})
              i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi h
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g'(j) \neq h'(j)
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \gt i
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi U
                      %mo ≠
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi h
                      %mo ′
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [g']_U \neq [h']_U
          %h3#RabinowitschTrick Rabinowitsch’s “trick”
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Rabinowitsch1930"} Rabinowitsch 1930
            showed how to deduce the Strong Nullstellensatz from the Weak Nullstellensatz. Often this is described as Rabinowitsch’s “trick” (i.e., something involving a stroke of cleverness), but see the remark below which places the trick conceptually within the general method of localization.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be algebraically closed and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subseteq k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
            be an ideal. To show that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ideal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Var
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msqrt
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ideal(Var(I)) = \sqrt{I}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
            vanishes at any point where all of a given set of polynomials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1, \ldots, f_s \in k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
            vanish. It suffices to show that for some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^r
            belongs to the ideal generated by the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
          %p
            Introduce a fresh variable
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_0, a_1, \ldots, a_n) \in k^{n+1}
            where the polynomials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - x_0 f, f_1, \ldots, f_s
            simultaneously vanish. By the Weak Nullstellensatz (Theorem
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#weak"}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = p_0(x)(1 - x_0 f) + p_1(x) f_1 + \ldots + p_s(x) f_s
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = (x_0, x_1, \ldots, x_n)
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x_0, x_1, \ldots, x_n] \to k(x_1, \ldots, x_n)
            sending
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ↦
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0 \mapsto 1/f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i \mapsto x_i
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq i \leq n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = \sum_{i=1}^s p_i(1/f, x_1, \ldots, x_n) f_i
          %p
            which, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is the highest degree of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
            appearing in a
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi r
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^r = \sum_{i=1}^s g_i f_i
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]
            by clearing denominators.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Proving that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msqrt
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in \sqrt{I}
              means we prove that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is nilpotent in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]/I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]/I
              with respect to the (image of the) multiplicative system
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1, f, \ldots, f^n, \ldots\}
              vanishes. Clearly we localize by inverting (the image of)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi I
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(k[x_1, \ldots, x_n]/I\right)[f^{-1}] = k[x_0, x_1, \ldots, x_n]/(I, 1 - x_0 f).
            %p
              Clearly
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Var
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Var(I, 1 - x_0 f) = \emptyset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (I, 1 - x_0 f)
              is improper, i.e., the localization vanishes.
          %h2#GeneralAbstract General abstract formulations
          %p
            By the discussion above at
            %em
              %a{:href => "#ExistenceOfPoints"} Existence of points
            it follows that phrased in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            over the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
          %p
            Motivated by this, in (
            %a{:href => "#Lawvere07"}> Lawvere 07, def. 2
            ) is a proposal for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            formulation of what constitutes a
            = succeed "," do
              %em Nullstellensatz
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            is a relative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            such that the terminal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            extended to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi coDisc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi \dashv Disc \dashv \Gamma \dashv coDisc)
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo ,
                  %mi coDisc
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                  %mo ↪
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc, coDisc \colon \mathbf{S}\hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            preserving
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            here induces a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ptp
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ptp \;\colon\; \Gamma \longrightarrow \Pi
          %p
            which deserves to be called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "cohesive+topos#CanonicalComparison"} points-to-pieces transformation
          %p
            Consider the condition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ptp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ptp
            is on every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            this means that “all pieces of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            have at least one point”. (See at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "cohesive+topos#PiecesHavePoints"} cohesive topos – Pieces have points
            %a{:href => "#Lawvere07"} Lawvere 07, def. 2 c)
            is also referred to as
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Nullstellensatz
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lawvere11"} Lawvere 11
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone11"} Johnstone 11
          %p
            For a detailed analysis of how this general abstract concept indeed captures the traditional meaning of
            = succeed "," do
              %em Nullstellensatz
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lawvere15"} Lawvere 15
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Menni"} Menni
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Tholen"} Tholen
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Hilbert"}> David Hilbert
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Über die vollen Invariantensysteme
              %strong 42
              (1893) 313–373 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01444162"}> doi:10.1007/BF01444162
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-52012-9_19"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-52012-9_19
          %p
            The
            = succeed ":" do
              %em Rabinowitsch trick
          %ul
            %li#Rabinowitsch1930
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juli+L.+Rabinowitsch"}> Juli L. Rabinowitsch
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Zum Hilbertschen Nullstellensatz
              %strong 102
              1 (1930) 520-520 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/bf01782361"}> doi:10.1007/bf01782361
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilbert's_Nullstellensatz"} Hilbert’s Nullstellensatz
          %h3#the_model_theoretic_perspective The model theoretic perspective
          %p
            In terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                %em On the transfer of an abstract Nullstellensatz
                , Comm. Alg.
                %strong 10
                (1982) pp.1891-1906.
            %li
              %p
                W. A. MacCaull,
                %em Hilbert’s Nullstellensatz revisited
                , JPAA
                %strong 54
                (1988) pp.289-297.
            %li
              %p
                V. Weispfenning,
                %em Nullstellensätze - a model theoretic framework
                , Z. Math. Logik Grundl. Math.
                %strong 23
                (1977) pp. 539-545.
          %h3#in_terms_of_cohesion In terms of cohesion
          %p
            Discussion of the Nullstellensatz in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em Axiomatic cohesion
                Theory and Applications of Categories, Vol. 19, No. 3 (2007) pp. 41–49. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/19/3/19-03.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Lawvere11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/52894/381"} MO comment on the general abstract Nullstellensatz
                (2011)
            %li#Lawvere15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+William+Lawvere"}> F. William Lawvere
                ,
                %em Birkhoff’s Theorem from a geometric
              %p
                perspective: A simple example_ , Categories and General Algebraic Structures with Applications, Vol. 4, No. 1 (2015) pp. 1–7. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cgasa.ir/pdf_12425_5ddf468d82aad53ce2e8ee88dd3bf84d.html"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Johnstone11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Remarks on punctual local connectedness
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/25/3/25-03abs.html"} TAC
            %li#RRZ04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marie+La+Palme+Reyes"}> Marie La Palme Reyes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gonzalo+E.+Reyes"} G. E. Reyes
                %em Generic Figures and their Glueings
                , Polimetrica Milano 2004. (pp.206-224)
            %li#Menni
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matias+Menni"}> Matias Menni
                ,
                %em The manifestation of Hilbert’s Nullstellensatz in Lawvere’s Axiomatic Cohesion
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~workct/slides/Menni.pdf"} pdf slides
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~workct/abstracts/Menni.pdf"} pdf abstract
            %li#Menni14a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mat%C3%ADas+Menni"}> Matías Menni
                ,
                %em Sufficient Cohesion over Atomic Toposes
                , Cah.Top.Géom.Diff.Cat.
                %strong LV
                (2014). (
                %a{:href => "https://sites.google.com/site/matiasmenni/SufCohesion12.pdf?attredirects=0"}> preprint
                )
            %li#Menni14b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mat%C3%ADas+Menni"}> Matías Menni
                ,
                %em Continuous Cohesion over Sets
                , TAC
                %strong 29
                no.20 (2014) pp.542-568. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/29/20/29-20.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Tholen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"}> Walter Tholen
                ,
                %em Nullstellen and Subdirect Representation
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.yorku.ca/~tholen/nullstMarch2013bis.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %h3#in_spectral_algebraic_geometry In spectral algebraic geometry
          %p
            For a version of the Nullstellensatz in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+algebraic+geometry"} spectral algebraic geometry
